<h1>About GatherPack</h1>

<%= render "definition" %>

<p class="lead">GatherPack wasn’t dreamed up in a pitch deck. It grew out of a decade of running a real volunteer organization — scattered spreadsheets, sticky notes, and a volunteer who got tired of hunting for the same answer twice.</p>

<section id="who" class="card" aria-labelledby="who-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="who-heading">Who’s behind it</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <div class="row g-4 align-items-center">
      <div class="col-12 col-md-8">
        <p>GatherPack is built by <a href="https://brad-thompson.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brad Thompson</a>, a volunteer web developer and mentor, together with students from the team itself. Brad’s day job is through <a href="https://sledgehammerinfosystems.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sledgehammer Infosystems</a>, which publishes and supports GatherPack and provides managed hosting for groups that prefer not to self-host.</p>
        <p class="mb-2">That lineage matters for E-E-A-T: the software comes from lived operational experience, not a lab. The predecessor ran a nonprofit’s daily operations for ten years; GatherPack is the rebuild done in the open.</p>
        <p class="mb-0 small text-muted">Author: <a href="https://brad-thompson.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brad Thompson</a> · Publisher: <a href="https://sledgehammerinfosystems.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sledgehammer Infosystems, LLC</a> · Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@gatherpack.com">hello@gatherpack.com</a> · Source: <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GatherPack/gatherpack</a></p>
